  "behavior": [
    "MlxModelSession::from_model attempts checked initial idle storage publication after its initial reset settles.",
    "The transition requires a healthy idle session, exclusive payload ownership, complete numerical nonstate inventory, certified empty decoder storage and exact loading-authority identity across the executable and initial operation history.",
    "The outer session field audit covers discovery declarations, deferred fingerprint paths/file metadata, capture layouts, state-residency accounting metadata, capabilities, failure strings and session authority; no additional numerical payload is owned there.",
    "Complete identity-based registration and native attachments finish before executable, payload and initial-reset loading handles retire. A local immutable owner guard spans the entire transition.",
    "Uncertified lazy helpers, missing source/processor/communication coverage, nonempty decoder storage or different operation authority preserve local loading handles. Registration or attachment errors likewise retain the original guard.",
    "Independent loading clones and native recovery keep exclusion even after local publication. Publication never clears a shared lease or authorizes a future operation.",
    "Ordinary operations reacquire model/context authority before native work. A live synthetic reservation rejects reset, token construction and an input factory without changing state or accounting. Raw output aliases retain the newly acquired owner after the session retires.",
    "The constructor does not repeat publication on an already promoted session. Test-only executable mutation accessors explicitly acquire unquoted authority after initial publication."
  ],
